{"name":"Stonewall","hex":"#807661","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Stonewall","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of stonewall (“alcoholic drink”)."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A series of riots in 1969 New York City, beginning with the patrons of the gay bar \"The Stonewall Inn\" resisting police arrest, which marked the beginning of the militant gay rights movement.","A nickname of Confederate general Thomas Jonathan Jackson."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Stonewall"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stone wall","blocks":[{"text":"Stone walls are a kind of masonry construction that has been used for thousands of years."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Belgorod_ua.jpg/330px-Belgorod_ua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stone_wall"},{"title":"Stonewalling","blocks":[{"text":"Stonewalling is a refusal to communicate or cooperate. Such behaviour occurs in situations such as interpersonal relationships, marriage counselling, diplomatic negotiations, politics and legal cases. Body language may indicate and reinforce this by avoiding contact and engagement with the other party. People use deflection in a conversation in order to render a conversation pointless and insignificant. Tactics in stonewalling include giving sparse, vague responses; refusing to answer questions; and responding to questions with additional questions. Stonewalling can be used as a stalling tactic rather than an avoidance tactic. In the original definition by John Gottman, in interpersonal relationships, it is an involuntary physiological condition where one's nervous system shuts down in response to being flooded, and it is part of the pursuer-withdrawer, or criticism-stonewalling cycle."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stonewalling"},{"title":"Stonewall (charity)","blocks":[{"text":"Stonewall Equality Limited, trading as Stonewall, is a lesbian, gay, bisexual and transgender (LGBTQ) rights charity in the United Kingdom. It is the largest LGBT rights organisation in Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Stonewall-Logo.png/330px-Stonewall-Logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stonewall_(charity)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/City_wall_close.jpg/500px-City_wall_close.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/City_wall_close.jpg/500px-City_wall_close.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"City wall in Worms, Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACity_wall_close.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Kumamoto_Castle_02n3200.jpg/500px-Kumamoto_Castle_02n3200.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Kumamoto_Castle_02n3200.jpg/1280px-Kumamoto_Castle_02n3200.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Kumamoto_Castle_02n3200.jpg/500px-Kumamoto_Castle_02n3200.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stone wall of Kumamoto Castle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKumamoto_Castle_02n3200.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Royal_Military_College_of_Canada_fence.jpg/330px-Royal_Military_College_of_Canada_fence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Royal_Military_College_of_Canada_fence.jpg/330px-Royal_Military_College_of_Canada_fence.